Z||000000||varnster||11-12-2000||05:38 PM||||I got my cruise control vacume tubing all<BR>screwed up, can some take a look at their<BR>87gt and let me know what tubing goes where<BR>especilly the tubing on the solinoid that is<BR>connected to the cruise control plunger thingamagig||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||11-12-2000||06:37 PM||||That's what I just did, an hour ago!<P>On mine (yes, a 1987 GT), the tube from the diaphragm thingamagig plugs into the left (driver's side) of the solenoid.  The other side (passenger side) just has a vent - no connection.  Maybe there <B>used</B> to be a little foam "sock" on there, or a line to the "clean" side of the air cleaner, but mine's just open to the atmosphere now.<P>Does that do ya  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ?   <P>||||reg||5
Z||000002||StuGood||11-12-2000||07:00 PM||||By the way, in case your solenoid is oriented differently than mine, there's an electrical connector in the "vent" end of the solenoid.  The tube from the diaphragm/plunger/thingy plugs into the other end.<P>FWIW, checked my 1988 four-cylinder Fiero, and it's plumbed exactly the same way as the GT...  except the '88 still has the foam "sock" on the vent end.    ||||reg||1
Z||000003||varnster||11-12-2000||07:08 PM||||I hooked it up just like you said,accept now<BR>its not shifting correcly its staying in first gear untill I let up on the gas. And<BR>their are 2 hose connections on the pasenger<BR>side of the solenoid, not just one,are both<BR>of yours vented to atmosphere, I dont think<BR>anything associated with this should effect<BR>the shifting of an automatic trany,should<BR>it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||11-12-2000||11:14 PM||||Uh, oh - now you've done it.  Sell your car immediately, before the fenders fall off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!<P>Please recheck the vacuum hoses for cracks and make sure they fit tightly over the fittings.  Might be a vacuum leak crept in.  The vacuum cans have been known to corrode and leak, too, I believe.<P>If you really think the cruise control is affecting the shifting, try pulling off the hose from the vacuum can (the one that runs to the metal line), and cap it off.  If the shifting goes back to normal, you know to start hunting for vacuum leaks in the cruise control hardware.||||reg||9
